    "exception": {
      "kind": "other",
      "authority": "User waiver dated 2026-09-13",
      "adoption": "Historical incidents for non-China companies may proceed when contained and remediated; current unresolved issues remain held.",
      "usefulness": "CircleCI user, project, pipeline, and workflow reads provide cheap authenticated CI inventory without triggering billed pipelines.",
      "incident": "On 4 January 2023 CircleCI disclosed a security incident. Malware on an engineer laptop stole a valid 2FA-backed SSO session on 16 December 2022. The actor accessed production systems and exfiltrated customer environment variables, tokens, and keys; encryption keys were extracted from a running process. Last unauthorized production activity was recorded 22 December 2022. Several customers later reported unauthorized third-party access using stolen secrets.",
      "remediation": "CircleCI shut down the compromised employee access on 4 January 2023, restricted production access, rotated customer-associated tokens (project API, personal API, GitHub OAuth, Bitbucket), partnered with AWS to notify customers of potentially affected AWS keys, and published a 13 January 2023 incident report asking customers to rotate remaining secrets and review logs from 21 December 2022.",
      "residualRisk": "Historical customer-secret exposure. Live authentication and current security posture are unverified.",
